        "name": "Kattarikuppe",
        "description": "<img src=\"https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3ADbDBKssyLt9p0T-2RATkwgmcyAeg1rco_23FTldhfeWCfPH03EpPR2V_sxNuWuwUD5hTt3OzidT-I1wpZPbZJFfoC-8--nKv0w9O_DuPVyc2CO_Edlsd-j0ufbkWUConaC01zwmUh4cjH6fchFvlOEhvfI93mESZc8JjR-cMDCF0GBiQfryrucKSFKdFyAGofZbcFUQVXA?authuser=0&fife=s16383\" height=\"200\" width=\"auto\" /><br><br>EC 9 An#: 28<br>Description of Installed Location in Historical Records: At Kattarikuppe (same hobli), near the chavadi within the village entrance to the south<br>Installation Date: 01/01/1380<br>Hobli (as recorded in EC): Sarjapura<br>Poster in Exhibition?: <br>Inscription language: Grantha & Tamil<br>Size: <br>Current Status: Intact (Dr Byrappa MG, Mythic Society Inscriptions Digital Conservation Team)<br>English translation of the Inscription: 28<br>Date about 1380 A.D.<br>(Tamil) – According to the order of ………… Nagana Odappa-udaiyar, ………………. Vana-udayiyar Kasar and the senabova Madi-siyar Kambayar, the superintendent of Erumarai-nadu, seem to have made a grant …………….. Naganna-udai …………………………… (Usual final imprecatory sentence).<br><br>Kannada Transliteration Of The Inscription: 28<br>ಅದೇ ಹೋಬಳಿ ಕತ್ತರಿಕುಪ್ಪೆ ಗ್ರಾಮಕ್ಕೆ ದಕ್ಷಿಣ ಊರಬಾಗಲವೊಳದಡೆ ಚಾವಡೀ ಬಳಿ.<br><br>ಅರವಕ್ಷರ<br>Tamil Transliteration Of The Inscription: <br>Telugu Transliteration Of The Inscription: <br>English Translation  Retyped By: arun kumar mr <mrarunakumar@rediffmail.com><br>English Transliteration  Retyped By: <br>Kannada Transliteration Retyped By: arun kumar mr <mrarunakumar@rediffmail.com><br>Photographs Provided By: Dr Byrappa MG, Mythic Society Inscriptions Digital Conservation Team<br>Latitude: 12.91559<br>Longitude: 77.76594<br><br><img src=\"https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3ADbDBKtGYhvBPmEc78ycN6rqtYa2DgADGWH7vKviJUUqn_l4RaaMU3yDr__VciohZlr5q_UPOBBNNofrEZ2uqc9zGFSCJbWS2WgSqV-ZdTU1c7wX9OtZRh36sZhUqa0KnMcjZeRGOnLPdDid-JZcDxshdpQfTuBkSVuorXMRDRvA4qtGK5azxngG1eFOL8t6mHm9zHRoQyk?authuser=0&fife=s16383\" height=\"200\" width