        "Epigraphia_Carnatica_Vol_9__Bangalore_Taluq_Inscription_Number": "15",
        "Hobli": "Bangalore (Pete & Cantt)",
        "Description_of_Installed_Location_in_Historical_Record": "At the same village, on a stone set up by the side of the house presented to the Somesvara temple by Saranga Sabhapati Mudaliar.",
        "English_Transliteration_Of_The_Inscription": "16\n At yelahanka (Yelahanka hobli), at the base of Garuda-kambha in front of the Gopala-Krishna\nSvasti sri S’aka-varsha savirada munura muvatta murane Vikriti-samvastarada Bhadrapada-sudha-trydasiyu Gurvaradalu rajadhiraja raja-paramesvara sri-ira-Deva-Raya-Odeyaru sakalasambrajyavan aluva kaladalu Bommanna-ayyagala dharmada sasanada Bammanna-Settiya magaz Macharusa-Settiyaru madisidaz dipa-maleya-kambhakke mangala maha sri\n",
