        "name": "Nagondahalli",
        "description": "Epigraphia Carnatica Vol 9, Bangalore Taluq Inscription Number: 42<br>Hobli: Vartur Hobli<br>Description of Installed Location in Historical Record: At Nagondahalli (same hobli), on a stone in Nagananaykanakote Bayiras field.<br>Installation Date: 01/01/0820<br>Inscription Language: Kannada<br>Size: 3'4\"x4'6\"<br>Current Status: Not traceable<br>English Translation Of The Inscription: 42<br><br>Date about 820 A.D.<br><br>Be it well .  For the setting up of ? Siva Bhima, the Ninety- two granted land (specified). Imprecation.<br>When Ra amalla- Permmanadi was ruling the Kingdom was this erected.<br><br>English Transliteration Of The Inscription: <br>Kannada Transliteration Of The Inscription: 42<br><br>ಅದೇ ಹೋಬಳಿ ನಾಗೊಂಡಹಳ್ಳಿ ಗ್ರಾಮಕ್ಕೆ ಪೂರ್ವ ನಾಗನಾಯ್ಕನಕೋಟೆ ಒಯಿರನ ಹೊಲದಲ್ಲಿ ನೆಟ್ಟಕಲ್ಲು <br><br>ಪ್ರಮಾಣ 3’4” x 4’6” <br>Tamil Transliteration Of The Inscription: NA<br>Telugu Transliteration Of The Inscription: NA<br>English Translation  Retyped By: Udaya Kumar P L <udayakumar.pl@gmail.com><br>English Transliteration  Retyped By: <br>Kannada Transliteration Retyped By: Udaya Kumar P L <udayakumar.pl@gmail.com><br>Photographs Provided By: Udaya Kumar P L <udayakumar.pl@gmail.com><br>Latitude: 12.9717122<br>Longitude: 77.7656258<br>Name*: <br>EC 9 Ht#: <br>Description of Installed Location in Historical Records: <br>Hobli (as recorded in EC): ",
