        "English_Transliteration_Of_The_Inscription": "60\nAt the same village, on a stone set up in the batayi land to the west.\n(grantha and Tamil characters).\nSvasti sri S’aka-varusham ayirattu-iranurr-embattettin mel sellaninra Isvara-samvatsarattu Ani-masa elan-diyadi purva-pakshattu Tri …………… Tingal kilamaiyum …………Pusattinal srimat-pra-dapa-ehchakravatti Hosala-vira-Vallal-Devar prithivi-rajyam-panniy-arulaninra kalattu Turavigali-nattavarum vira-Vallala-Devar Kumara ……… ya-nayakkanum Turaivali-nattu sima-samayattn………………….. vanda.. raiyum….. kk-adaitta naujay punjainal-pai-ellayum mel nokkina maramum kil nokkina kinarum .. .. .. ra-purvam-aga chamdraditya-varai sellakadavad-aga Vangi-purattu Kaikula. Yarullittar pang-ettu S’ribhasai Rama-piran pang-irandu Karambisettu purushottaman pangu nalu Vangipurattu Andavilil pang-onru Maruti pang-onru ivargalukku sarva-manyam-aga-kkudutom inda dharmmattukku lamghanam-panninavan Gamagi-kkaraiyil kural-pasuvai-kkonran papatte poga-sadavan svabham astu (usual final verse)\n",
