        "name": "Belur  (can be visited only on Monday mornings)",
        "description": "<img src=\"https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3ADbDBKvxwdRIA05VC9Uyr8fLBAvFzlbe5md4tJ5g5CwDfBlhphrcknyu3QkOmSidQTR0Ru-t-i6VzezX-po8Rvc-MVZIkh2xkPhnPBnLVQ7D4n3vi_ProifkwxSG_I5HbHJOZJGgM-QJHr3Zqmyj3ujXwYlQKOlQv474cKkym67PSfGSRFuWojCG3rsze7UL-Yj8ZmbtbRn2?authuser=0&fife=s16383\" height=\"200\" width=\"auto\" /><br><br>Epigraphia Carnatica Vol 9, Bangalore Taluq Inscription Number: 72<br>Hobli: Agara Hobli<br>Description of Installed Location in Historical Record: At Belur (same hobli),on a stone setup in front of the Someshvara Temple<br>Installation Date: 01/01/1350<br>Inscription Language: Grantha & Tamil<br>Size: 3'x2'6\"<br>Current Status: Intact<br>English Translation Of The Inscription: 72<br><br>Date? About 1350 A.D<br><br>(Tamil)- We, Pamma-battar and Sembu-battar, having received full payment in gold, gave to Pillaiyar full possession of the land and the house which had been ours for a long time and transferred to him the service for fifteen days……… in the temple of this god, which we had purchased form kulainja-battar.<br>The signatures of Pamma-battar and Sembu-battar. Witnesses to the grant: Varadi-deva-kon and Sokkannan.<br><br><br>English Transliteration Of The Inscription: 72<br>At Ibbaluru (same hobli), on a stone set up in fron of the Somesvara temple. (Grantha nnd Tmil characters).<br>Svasti sri Talu .. kKulainja-bttar pakkal i-nnayanar koyilil nangal kondudaiyom-ana muppadu vattattu padinainju nalum munnalil.. lla mannum manaiyum Pillaiyarku pponn-ara kkondu mann-ara-kkudutton Pamma-battar S’embu-battaromippadikku Pamma-battar S’embu-battar eluttu ippatti ariven Varadi devakon ippatti ariven S’okkannanyena.<br><br>Kannada Transliteration Of The Inscription: 72<br><br>ಅದೇ ಹೋಬಳಿ ಬೇಲೂರು ಸೋಮೇಶ್ವರ ದೇವಾಲಯದ ಮುಂದೆ ನೆಟ್ಟಿರುವದು <br><br>ಗ್ರಂಥ ಮತ್ತು ಅರವಕ್ಷರ<br><br>ಪ್ರಮಾಣ 3’ x 2’6”<br>Tamil Transliteration Of The Inscription: Please help improve this map by providing us this. Please retype in Tamil the text of the inscription shown in the accompanying photos and email it to InscriptionStonesofBangalore@gmail.com. Thanks !<br>Telugu Transliteration Of The Inscription: NA<br>English Translation  Retyped By: Udaya Kumar P L <udayakumar.pl@gmail.com><br>English Transliteration  Retyped By: <br>Kannada Transliteration Retyped By: Udaya Kumar P L <udayakumar.pl@gmail.com><br>Photographs Provided By: Udaya Kumar P L <udayakumar.pl@gmail.com><br>Latitude: 12.94196<br>Longitude: 77.6668387<br>Name*: <br>EC 9 Ht#: <br>Description of Installed Location in Historical Records: <br>Hobli (as recorded in EC): <br><br><img src=\"https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3ADbDBKs92oluW8b3yYRBaECzVTR2E9dQKUJ6vi58YgpRwSVkZNgepACip5MBFwM-MrgW8ZsQPnTl5sM7GtKk-SSCEex2Vp3Oq0zWFvFZeerubBHvRgTw91r7b8e-e3tCuXlSvPsyIgnT9_K_5CvkD_6qwYv4jW0xJA9F0FD39vVc58wEUBHq_rv030LxYjnlAFvDER6YQCne?authuser=0&fife=s16383\" height=\"200\" width=\"auto\" />",
        "tessellate": "-1",
        "extrude": "0",
        "visibility": "-1",
        "Description_of_Installed_Location_in_Historical_Records": "",
        "Installation_Date": "01/01/1350",
