      "properties": {
        "name": "Kempapura",
        "description": "<img src=\"https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3ADbDBKuXogKZN0cDzS5MMlWMsqsWfgfAGJ3ny5z6s9LBA8nQFTpOkOiyA-3Y5Rx2WYzKcwMc-mq0vyK297VBO6YA0O3XurNQvzctkaOOSlx02PtIRCq3rHYPIJTjVUBnawXiO4ENKdOHBl12LMUDXykbhDeiyc8pTx47_f9HmhExKIPniuw8SGAOqPf7zDrkW9zrcR3UpTw?authuser=0&fife=s16383\" height=\"200\" width=\"auto\" /><br><br>Epigraphia Carnatica Vol 9, Bangalore Taluq Inscription Number: 76<br>Hobli: Agara Hobli<br>Description of Installed Location in Historical Record: At Kempapura (same hobli), in pujari Lahshmayya's inam land.<br>Installation Date: 01/01/1306<br>Inscription Language: Grantha & Tamil<br>Size: 4'x3'<br>Current Status: Not traceable<br>English Translation Of The Inscription: 76<br><br>Date 1306 A.D<br><br>(Tamil)- While the pratapa-chakravartti sri-Posala-vira-Vallala-Devarasan was pleased to rule the earth-<br>(From the date specified), we granted, with pouring of water, as a deva-dana for the god Villisvaram-udaiyar of Villagamundanpalli, The village of Sattaidevanpalli in Erumarai-nadu, the tank Avanjikattu of the village end all the wet and dry lands adjoining the village, including the wells underground and the trees overground within their four boundaries, in order to provide for worship, sacred service and offerings of rice. This village shall continue as a sarva-manya. (usual final imprecatory sentence).<br>Villa-For victory to the sword and arm of the pratapa-chakravatti vira-vallala-devar- We, the inhabitants of ku…..nadu and Periya-nadu….., remitted certain taxes (named))………,<br>English Transliteration Of The Inscription: <br>Kannada Transliteration Of The Inscription: 76<br>ಅದೇ ಹೋಬಳಿ ಕೆಂಪಾಪುರದಲ್ಲಿ ಪೂಜಾರಿ ಲಕ್ಷ್ಮಯ್ಯನ ಇನಾಂ ಭೂಮಿಯಲ್ಲಿ <br><br>ಗ್ರಂಥ ಮತ್ತು ಅರವಕ್ಷರ - ಪ್ರಮಾಣ 4’ x 3’<br>Tamil Transliteration Of The Inscription: Please help improve this map by providing us this. Please retype in Tamil the text of the inscription shown in the accompanying photos and email it to InscriptionStonesofBangalore@gmail.com. Thanks !<br>Telugu Transliteration Of The Inscription: NA<br>English Translation  Retyped By: Udaya Kumar P L <udayakumar.pl@gmail.com><br>English Transliteration  Retyped By: <br>Kannada Transliteration Retyped By: Udaya Kumar P L <udayakumar.pl@gmail.com><br>Photographs Provided By: Udaya Kumar P L <udayakumar.pl@gmail.com><br>Latitude: 12.9447686<br>Longitude: 77.6740395<br>Name*: <br>EC 9 Ht#: <br>Description of Installed Location in Historical Records: <br>Hobli (as recorded in EC): <br><br><img src=\"https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3ADbDBKvAa7L2Q9nbkpP3lCf_qOnFLevC0PATfkIpUIbSoNdyaI-drPloogo0PPbl7IXqb4yA2UP8ZERppFPIw49ndNlPVcrE3NRrLuDGB9EybLiSYwy4H0yIYJgHamyW5Y_660Edu3W6Tvjlmzl07QrQFSljMGLVi9ri8ZSfh2Ci96bVZ2ZTY1Uye4shsEOPaWBJa_ZjZ2I?authuser=0&fife=s16383\" height=\"200\" width=\"auto\" />",
        "tessellate": "-1",
        "extrude": "0",
        "visibility": "-1",
        "Description_of_Installed_Location_in_Historical_Records": "",
        "Installation_Date": "01/01/1306",
