        "Description_of_Installed_Location_in_Historical_Record": "On a stone brought from the same village to the Bangalore museum.",
        "English_Transliteration_Of_The_Inscription": "81\nOn a stone brought from the same village to the Bangalore Museum.\n\nSvasti sri S’akabda 1286 neya S’obhakritu-sam| Jyeshta-su 11 Bu | srimanu-maha-mandalesvaram ari-raya-vibhada bhashege tappuva rayara ganda sri-vira-Bkkanna-Vodeyara kumara Kampanna-Vodeyaru Mulubagila-pattanadalu pruthvi-rajyam geyutt ire a-Kampanna-Vodeyara kumara Kamaiyya-Nayakaru yi-rajyada gavundugala mundittu Elahanka-nada Allala-jiyana maga Tanniyappange sila-sasanava madikotta kramav ent endade.. nti-nada tenkana-bageya Torevali-nada Belarttaye mula gadde beddalu chatus-simey enulladaru sarvamanyada kodagey Agi Chandra-dityar-ullana-bra saluvant Agi.. sila-sasanava madikottevu mangala maha sri ||\n\n\nMythic Society Inscription 3D Scanning Re-Reading\n\n1)svasti śrī śakābda 1286\n2)nĕya śobhakṛtu saṃ| jyeṣṭa śu11\n3)bu| śrī manumahāmaṃḍal̤eśvaraṃ arirā\n4)ya vibhāḍa bhāṣĕgĕ tappuva rāyaragaṃḍa\n5)śrī vīrabukkaṇṇavŏḍĕyara kumāra kaṃpaṇṇa\n6)vŏḍĕyaru mul̤ubāgila paṭṭaṇadalu pru\n7)thvirājyaṃgĕyuttiralu kaṃpaṇṇa vŏḍĕyara\n8)kumāra kāmaiyanāykaru yī rājyada gavu\n9)ṃḍugal̤a muṃdiṭṭu ĕlahakkanāḍa allā\n10)l̤ajīyana maga taṇṇiyappaṃgĕ śilāśāsanava\n11)māḍikŏṭa kramavĕṃtĕdaḍĕ saṇṇĕnāḍa tĕ\n12)ṃkaṇa bāgĕya tŏṟĕval̤ināḍa bĕl̤attūranū\n13)yī vūra gaddĕ bĕddalu catussīmĕ yenu\nhiṃbhāga\n14)l̤l̤adanū sarvamānyada kŏḍagĕyāgi\n15)caṃdrādityarul̤l̤aṃnabarasaluvaṃ\n16)tāgi śilā śāsanava māḍikkŏ\n17)ṭṭĕvu maṃgal̤a mahāśrīḥ |\n",
