      "properties": {
        "name": "Hongasandra ",
        "description": "<img src=\"https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3ADbDBKtx26HbGBMZNbj4i6GDfQjY_MCVrRMg7tjaKeuex3IPakNnfsqoxkS8Znsm1N1LKJ5z20dNsR_oM6LkKIio4c4vEp-ie0cLOeMRVoRNss2gyds5Nv7aM9wj7dhAWfCbxEEjliFROXmVrt3fH4pDHjCM9x93MIXPf1_qgCVCd6iuuWgHJMl-PsNn028OdkKr6rZ1dfM?authuser=0&fife=s16383\" height=\"200\" width=\"auto\" /><br><br>Epigraphia Carnatica Vol 9, Bangalore Taluq Inscription Number: 100<br>Hobli: Begur Hobli<br>Description of Installed Location in Historical Record: At the same village, on a stone in Survey 50, Gopaliyengars palya<br>Installation Date: 01/01/1294<br>Inscription Language: Grantha & Tamil<br>Size: 6'X3'2\"<br>Current Status: Not traceble<br>English Translation Of The Inscription: 100<br><br>Date 1294 A.D<br><br>(Tamil) – In the 40th year of the reign of the universal emperor sri-Poysala-vira-Iramana-Devar-charitable gift, for feeding Brahmans, Anumasamuttiram and Unangimaran-kuttai, situated within the boundaries of Veppur, together with the adjoining wet and dry lands with their four boundaries, including the wells underground and the trees overground, to the 28 men of this village who should conduct the duties of tanapatis..(Then follow names of the 28 men).<br>I, Tamattamavar, made the above grant, with pouring of water, as a charitable gift, to the 28 men, with the right to sell or give away (the lands), for the benefit of the king’s sacred body and of myself.<br>This charity shall last as long as the moon and the sun. (Usual final imprecatory sentence).<br><br>English Transliteration Of The Inscription: <br>Kannada Transliteration Of The Inscription: 100<br><br>ಅದೇ ಸ್ಥಳದಲ್ಲಿ<br><br>ಗ್ರಂಥ ಮತ್ತು ಅರವಕ್ಷರ <br><br>ಪ್ರಮಾಣ 6’ x 3’<br>Tamil Transliteration Of The Inscription: Please help improve this map by providing us this. Please retype in Tamil the text of the inscription shown in the accompanying photos and email it to InscriptionStonesofBangalore@gmail.com. Thanks !<br>Telugu Transliteration Of The Inscription: NA<br>English Translation  Retyped By: Udaya Kumar P L <udayakumar.pl@gmail.com><br>English Transliteration  Retyped By: <br>Kannada Transliteration Retyped By: Udaya Kumar P L <udayakumar.pl@gmail.com><br>Photographs Provided By: Udaya Kumar P L <udayakumar.pl@gmail.com><br>Latitude: 12.8926453<br>Longitude: 77.6372082<br>Name*: <br>EC 9 Ht#: <br>Description of Installed Location in Historical Records: <br>Hobli (as recorded in EC): ",
        "tessellate": "-1",
        "extrude": "0",
        "visibility": "-1",
        "Description_of_Installed_Location_in_Historical_Records": "",
