        "description": "Epigraphia Carnatica Vol 9, Bangalore Taluq Inscription Number: 126<br>Hobli: Yasavantapura Hobli<br>Description of Installed Location in Historical Record: At Yasavantapura (Yasavantapura hobli) on a stone in Rudrappa's field to the south-east.<br>Installation Date: 01/01/1650<br>Inscription Language: Kannada<br>Size: 2'6\"X2'<br>Current Status: Not traceable<br>English Translation Of The Inscription: 126<br><br>Date about 1650 A.D<br><br>The Elavakka-nad prabhu….? Chennaya-Gauda granted to Yesavantapura Kempa-Gauda as a kodage…..<br><br>English Transliteration Of The Inscription: <br>Kannada Transliteration Of The Inscription: 126<br><br>ಅದೇ ಗ್ರಾಮಕ್ಕೆ ಅಗ್ನೇಯದಲ್ಲಿ ರುದ್ರಪ್ಪನ ಹೊಲದಲ್ಲಿ <br><br>ಪ್ರಮಾಣ 2’6” x 2’<br><br>ಎಲವಕನ್ನಡಪ್ರಭು <br>ಬ .. ರವರದಶ್ರೀಮನು ..<br>ಬೆಂಯಗಉಡರು <br>ಪುರದಕೆಂಪಗ <br>ಉಡರಿಗೆಕೊಟ್ಟಕೊ <br>ಡಗೆ <br><br>Tamil Transliteration Of The Inscription: NA<br>Telugu Transliteration Of The Inscription: NA<br>English Translation  Retyped By: Udaya Kumar P L <udayakumar.pl@gmail.com><br>English Transliteration  Retyped By: <br>Kannada Transliteration Retyped By: Udaya Kumar P L <udayakumar.pl@gmail.com><br>Photographs Provided By: Udaya Kumar P L <udayakumar.pl@gmail.com><br>Latitude: 13.019857<br>Longitude: 77.562429<br>Name*: <br>EC 9 Ht#: <br>Description of Installed Location in Historical Records: <br>Hobli (as recorded in EC): ",
