      "properties": {
        "name": "Dyvasandra",
        "description": "<img src=\"https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3ADbDBKs3ohGsXusSkpuOY11Hqm7_oTmzG_RIt6J2bgQ5akO3zC5qTtiTIqwKEXpueZtMbm3IkgRQsPBCjngWUCxGwj5yCrAu91UWbkMmo6uekCfhxhiW4YNV0Rta9OAZOoyrbj_xaK8nArYlVqircGdMqye2XZu1M6Ft7Q9IG9lxvIKalxvqA4QT2XB7Id0QuchsSuLqRU4?authuser=0&fife=s16383\" height=\"200\" width=\"auto\" /><br><br>Epigraphia Carnatica Vol 9, Bangalore Taluq Inscription Number: 132<br>Hobli: Yasavantapura Hobli<br>Description of Installed Location in Historical Record: At the bechirakh village Dyvasandra (same hobli), on a stone set up in front of the ruined Anjaneya temple.<br>Installation Date: 01/01/1376<br>Inscription Language: Grantha & Tamil<br>Size: 5'6\"x4'3\"<br>Current Status: Not traceable<br>English Translation Of The Inscription: 132.<br>Date 1376 A.D<br>(Tamil)- While the maha-mandalesvara, destroyer of hostile kings, champion over kings who break their word, lord of the eastern southern western and northern oceans, Suratrana (sultan) of the Hindu Rajas, the maharaja paramesvara sri-vira-Bukkanna-udaiyar was pleased to rate the earth-<br>(On the date specified), I- the maha samantadhipathi, champion over the three kings, champion over kings who break their word, Mayalaya-nayakkar’s son Devaya-Nayakkan- granted, with pouring of water, to continue as a sarva-manya for as long as the moon and the sun endure, certain lands (specified) in Devasamudra, alias ………………palli, of Ilaippakka-nadu, to a number of Brahmans of various gotras. (Usual final imprecatory sentences and final Sanskrit verse).<br><br>English Transliteration Of The Inscription: <br>Kannada Transliteration Of The Inscription: 132<br><br>ಅದೇ ಗ್ರಾಮದ ಬೇಟೆರಾಖ್ ದ್ಯಾವಸಂದ್ರ ಗ್ರಾಮದ ಆಚಿಜನೇಯನ ಪಾಳು ದೇವಸ್ಥಾನದ ಮುಂದೆ ನೆಟ್ಟ ಕಲ್ಲು.<br><br>ಗ್ರಂಥ ಮತ್ತು ಅರವಕ್ಷರ - ಪ್ರಮಾಣ 5’6” x 4’<br>Tamil Transliteration Of The Inscription: Please help improve this map by providing us this. Please retype in Tamil the text of the inscription shown in the accompanying photos and email it to InscriptionStonesofBangalore@gmail.com. Thanks !<br>Telugu Transliteration Of The Inscription: NA<br>English Translation  Retyped By: Udaya Kumar P L <udayakumar.pl@gmail.com><br>English Transliteration  Retyped By: <br>Kannada Transliteration Retyped By: Udaya Kumar P L <udayakumar.pl@gmail.com><br>Photographs Provided By: Udaya Kumar P L <udayakumar.pl@gmail.com><br>Latitude: 13.027586<br>Longitude: 77.572481<br>Name*: <br>EC 9 Ht#: <br>Description of Installed Location in Historical Records: <br>Hobli (as recorded in EC): <br><br><img src=\"https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3ADbDBKtAESplcD1SgmqtMvlk3QUwZS7sE1aQPvMXA8VxBcSj5fZKPW-YXcArkqFo5mZc9xMHk4mQcGIcXp1OCgruuBAUoVWNbba_SxIH-AOA6LJnRc9nCO_A4Qpe9tV-14TZUobuda8Qedg_0UPLx4NQOP3BF_wxM3wA0h-cjZVKTwFQEebsvvxOaMf9IPDR5-aztcWF1Lqb?authuser=0&fife=s16383\" height=\"200\" width=\"auto\" /><br><br><img src=\"https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3ADbDBKvcmwHgkX6rVXBRywNLoU-yjXN5IHRPZB16OJL48o1Av1gHQe2mjYJFtfUrDe4DXulsEByzbTvpuhs_pVl2miT9fpryiH9B0LMRs0pHctg7nILfNurwGVsBnvAHQ6YL4eiEkjDIFVNeSPZX7OK-WTgYkPY9Sv4miuDrZZ1-LhSlTehLmEaoCS0z6spk3zu6cxeE__Am?authuser=0&fife=s16383\" height=\"200\" width=\"auto\" /><br><br><img src=\"https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3ADbDBKu-XBGXlJYJytOgaYl4lB5Cn_Xk7bu8Ee0mWOpik23h2VBMrgYkl9TV4Vs-LOLUxwghpzqXUmM5ToCsbkmT7KGC6zC_A9GhDY5idVRIH5if1rreIKv1hbwcVuAIwsGLh4R40nAjcz_ga8Vr3uQ6dsKN8xO6Fbe3sr-XkiYSJRwAGMEyiynXkWD6g8XwWwFGq0quFncZ?authuser=0&fife=s16383\" height=\"200\" width=\"auto\" />",
