        "English_Transliteration_Of_The_Inscription": "133\nAt Vibhutipura (same hobli), on a stone set up in the land belonging to the matha. (Grantha & Tamil characters)\nSvasti srima-pratapa-chakravatti sri-Posala-vira-Villala-Devar valukun-dolukku nanraga .. Vallappa-dennakkarku nanrgavum manu-mahaprasayitta Ninran Masandi-nattu Menmugattu nattu-nayagan-jeyar S’embi-devarum Villa-gamundar S’anda-gamunda Veppuran Tanma. Siyar ullitta nattavarun-Govandiyum Vachchi-devarku-ttana-pramanam-panni-kkudutta parisavadu Plavanga-varusha-mudal Peru-Erumukk-adai… ppulattu-kkadu…. Tti-kkaruvittu ur-katti eriyu manal-olukki-kkatti Vachchidevarpuram enra per-akku.. .. .. ivv-urka adetta nanjai punjai narpal ellaryu mada-ppuram aga ivarku-chchantraditta-varai sarva-maniyam-aga-chchellakkadavad-aga vittom ivv-anaiverum inda-ttanmattukku ilanganam-panuinar udagil Gengai-kkaraiyil kurar-pasuvai-kkonra pavan golvar ivai ninrar eluttu nattu-kkanakkan Periyapillai eluttu.\n",
