      "properties": {
        "name": "Kacharkanahalli",
        "description": "<img src=\"https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3ADbDBKuxxLewAV3k2kmULV2zAe0bBEJD_28QZZrAdlylH0zhNtocjfNpnoQq1rJc775rTWL18_MbIel0HfjOl8o952XlWIiiS-AKbbmt_IfnEUVZEKQpdLWz5VW0q3DLkBzTvYn5yZQ84pc_fE_7hd2pp14q2y_KDxrG6fZ2R3lav23dcE2_aDen5OqJYzS03NxfZDMs8BI?authuser=0&fife=s16383\" height=\"200\" width=\"auto\" /><br><br>Epigraphia Carnatica Vol 9, Bangalore Taluq Inscription Number: 139a<br>Hobli: Yasavantapura Hobli<br>Description of Installed Location in Historical Record: At Kacharakanahalli (Esvanchapura hobli), on the west basement of the Sivanisvara temple<br>Installation Date: 01/01/1237<br>Inscription Language: Grantha & Tamil<br>Size: <br>Current Status: Not traceable<br>English Translation Of The Inscription: 139a<br>Date ? 1237 A.D<br>(Tamil) – During the rule of the emperor of the whole world Poysala-vira-Narasinga-Devar-in the time of Mnnimanavadai-udai-gandan Sikka-devar of Ilaippakka nadu, I, periya Treloka-settiyan, built (in the year specified) the tower of the temple of the god Sivanisvaram-udaiyar, and granted some land, exempt from taxes, to Sola-bhatta’s son Kanka-bettan. I, Vairi-battan, had the work of the vimana done…………………………..<br><br>English Transliteration Of The Inscription: <br>Kannada Transliteration Of The Inscription: <br>Tamil Transliteration Of The Inscription: Please help improve this map by providing us this. Please retype in Tamil the text of the inscription shown in the accompanying photos and email it to InscriptionStonesofBangalore@gmail.com. Thanks !<br>Telugu Transliteration Of The Inscription: NA<br>English Translation  Retyped By: Udaya Kumar P L <udayakumar.pl@gmail.com><br>English Transliteration  Retyped By: <br>Kannada Transliteration Retyped By: Udaya Kumar P L <udayakumar.pl@gmail.com><br>Photographs Provided By: Udaya Kumar P L <udayakumar.pl@gmail.com><br>Latitude: 13.0189931<br>Longitude: 77.6261874<br>Name*: <br>EC 9 Ht#: <br>Description of Installed Location in Historical Records: <br>Hobli (as recorded in EC): ",
        "tessellate": "-1",
        "extrude": "0",
        "visibility": "-1",
        "Description_of_Installed_Location_in_Historical_Records": "",
        "Installation_Date": "01/01/1237",
        "Hobli__as_recorded_in_EC_": "",
        "Inscription_language": "Grantha & Tamil",
        "Size": "",
        "Current_Status": "Not traceable",
        "English_translation_of_the_Inscription": "139a\nDate ? 1237 A.D\n(Tamil) – During the rule of the emperor of the whole world Poysala-vira-Narasinga-Devar-in the time of Mnnimanavadai-udai-gandan Sikka-devar of Ilaippakka nadu, I, periya Treloka-settiyan, built (in the year specified) the tower of the temple of the god Sivanisvaram-udaiyar, and granted some land, exempt from taxes, to Sola-bhatta’s son Kanka-bettan. I, Vairi-battan, had the work of the vimana done…………………………..\n",
        "Kannada_Transliteration_Of_The_Inscription": "",
        "Tamil_Transliteration_Of_The_Inscription": "Please help improve this map by providing us this. Please retype in Tamil the text of the inscription shown in the accompanying photos and email it to InscriptionStonesofBangalore@gmail.com. Thanks !",
        "Telugu_Transliteration_Of_The_Inscription": "NA",
